    "name_suffix": "_2026",
    "teacher_markdown": "- **Reinforce style vs. structure.**  \r\n  This level focuses on *style* (colors, fonts, spacing, visual consistency), not changing the page structure.\r\n\r\n- **Watch for under-specific prompts.**  \r\n  If students write something vague like “make it look modern,” push them to include:\r\n  - Specific brand colors  \r\n  - Specific fonts (or a clear font style)  \r\n  - Which sections must look consistent across both pages  \r\n\r\n- **Ensure they generate a separate CSS file.**  \r\n  AI may place styles directly inside the HTML unless students clearly state they want:\r\n  > “Generate a separate CSS file and link it to both HTML pages.”\r\n\r\n- **Address the “If it looks good, it must be correct” misconception.**  \r\n  Encourage students to preview both pages and ask:\r\n  - Is the text easy to read?  \r\n  - Do the colors have enough contrast?  \r\n  - Does this match the mood board from the previous level?\r\n  - What happens if you resize the page to a smaller screen?\r\n\r\n- **Connect back to planning.**  \r\n  Remind students they already defined their styling goals, constraints, and possible problems and that now they are translating that thinking into CSS.",
